  "steps": [
    "Heat the olive oil in a heavy pan over medium-high heat. Season the chuck roast generously with salt and pepper and sear on all sides until deeply browned.",
    "Move the roast to the slow cooker and top with the sliced onions.",
    "Add the red wine, rosemary, garlic paste, anchovies, beef stock, a good pinch of salt, plenty of black pepper, the bay leaves and a splash of Worcestershire.",
    "Cook on low for 8 hours, until the beef shreds easily. Remove the herbs and bay leaves and shred the meat in the juices.",
    "Mix the butter, garlic and parsley and spread it generously over the cut sides of the rolls. Toast under the broiler or in a hot oven until golden.",
    "Stir together the horseradish, grated garlic, mayonnaise, sour cream and pepper for the sauce.",
    "Spread horseradish sauce on the toasted rolls and pile on the shredded beef.",
    "Top with cheese and bake at 400°F for about 5 minutes, until melted.",
    "Ladle some of the cooking liquid into small bowls for dipping and serve right away."
  ],
  "equipment": [
    "slow cooker"
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Get a hard sear on the roast before it goes in; it builds the flavor of the broth.",
    "Check the beef near the end; it can need longer than expected to shred.",
    "Toast the garlic bread well so it stays crisp when dipped."
  ],
